{
  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits a persistent upward bias when the recent price trend is downward or flat; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 1.5% to 3%.",
    "When sentiment history shows mixed signals (positive and negative values) within the last 5 days, the model fails to capture immediate mean reversion, resulting in a systematic overestimation of volatility recovery.",
    "The model ignores short-term spikes in price (e.g., >4% moves) as drivers for future growth; true outcomes often reverse these spikes immediately, whereas forecasts assume continuation.",
    "Forecasts are overly smooth and lack the jaggedness of actual market behavior; apply a correction factor that increases variance and reduces expected returns by approximately 2-3 EUR per day during high-sentiment noise periods.",
    "When the last 3 days show a downtrend with neutral sentiment, the model incorrectly predicts a stabilization or slight uptick, while true outcomes continue to decline or consolidate at lower levels."
  ]
}
